WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.470
I'm very excited to meet you.

2
00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.700
Yeah, thanks for having us.

3
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.533
Yeah, thank you.

4
00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:06.750
Michael, will you tell us what happened?

5
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.100
Yeah, we were on our way back

6
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.080 line:15%
from a mass vaccination clinic

7
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.880 line:15%
that we actually had to shut down early

8
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.020 line:15%
because of severe weather.

9
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.310 line:15%
And we apparently didn't get out quite early enough,

10
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.800
because we wound up being stuck on a mountain top

11
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.320
because a snow storm and a jackknifed trailer.

12
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.710
So we had six doses left over,

13
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.460
that we couldn't use before we ran out the door

14
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.750
and we had people lined up to get 'em

15
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.300
but we just couldn't get to 'em in time.

16
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.240
So we had to make the decision in the moment

17
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.018 line:15%
and we decided it was better to use them then and there,

18
00:00:39.018 --> 00:00:40.180 line:15%
on the side of the road

19
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.830 line:15%
than it was to let 'em go to waste.

20
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.700
And Michael and Leah, really quickly,

21
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.070
what was that conversation like?

22
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.770
You're like, "okay, let's just find arms and people,

23
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.950
and tell our story and get this done

24
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.540
and not waste these precious vaccines."

25
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.170
What, what, what, what do you say?

26
00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.840
It was interesting having those conversations.

27
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.690
Internally, the first thing we asked was, is this safe?

28
00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.980
We had a doctor on staff.

29
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.770
We had an ambulance with us at the time.

30
00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.240
And as soon as we got the thumbs up from them,

31
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.870
I said, okay, let's go.

32
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.310
And we all zipped up our coats

33
00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.060
and started walking through the snow.

34
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.870
And Leah you were actually the one

35
00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.300
administering the vaccine.

36
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.500
What was that like?

37
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.680 line:15%
Oh, we had a pretty wide spectrum of reactions.

38
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.710 line:15%
This part of the country, there's some vaccine hesitancy.

39
00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.830
So most people just politely declined, but of course,

40
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.170
six people were excited about it.

41
00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.720
And we were able to give those six people vaccines.

42
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.380
Among them was this guy that was like so ecstatic.

43
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.110
He jumped out of his car practically

44
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.790
and ripped off his shirt.

45
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.650 line:15%
We also had a Deputy Sheriff from our county

46
00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.690 line:15%
who was trying to come to the mass vaccination event

47
00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.900 line:15%
to get her vaccine, but she was too late, she missed it.

48
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.630
And so we were able to give her a vaccine, too.

49
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:54.230
Well, I am really, really, really grateful

50
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.350
that you were able to spring into action.

51
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.050
I'm so beyond impressed with you guys

52
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.170
and I know everybody else is, too.

53
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.369
And thank you for your service.

54
00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:07.952
(upbeat music)

